
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F : Points
AB ⟂ AC [00]
AB = AC [01]
D,B,C are collinear [02]
DC = DB [03]
CE = CA [04]
B,E,C are collinear [05]
AF = AD [06]
B,F,A are collinear [07]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. AB = AC [01] & DC = DB [03] ⇒  BC ⟂ AD [08]
002. D,B,C are collinear [02] & BC ⟂ AD [08] & AB ⟂ AC [00] ⇒  ∠CAB = ∠ADC [09]
003. AB = AC [01] ⇒  ∠CBA = ∠ACB [10]
004. D,B,C are collinear [02] & ∠CBA = ∠ACB [10] ⇒  ∠CBA = ∠ACD [11]
005. ∠CAB = ∠ADC [09] & ∠CBA = ∠ACD [11] (Similar Triangles)⇒  CA:CB = AD:AC [12]
006. D,B,C are collinear [02] & DC = DB [03] ⇒  D is midpoint of BC [13]
007. AB ⟂ AC [00] & D is midpoint of BC [13] ⇒  BD = AD [14]
008. CA:CB = AD:AC [12] & BD = AD [14] & EC = AC [04] & BA = AC [01] & AF = AD [06] ⇒  BC:CE = BA:AF [15]
009. BC:CE = BA:AF [15] & B,E,C are collinear [05] & B,F,A are collinear [07] ⇒  CA ∥ EF [16]
010. AB ⟂ AC [00] & AC ∥ EF [16] ⇒  BA ⟂ FE
